    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "289645d5_f6a254e0",
        "filename": "python/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_delete_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000472
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T10:23:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. While provisioning a subscriber will create these ME\u0027s and while removing subscriber will remove them.",
      "parentUuid": "678c7a4b_918842bb",
      "revId": "435d5541dcc6a0624aa0dd880eaf38f9dc414a44",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9263e6f_2c66164a",
        "filename": "python/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_delete_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000218
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T18:07:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But tp_delete runs when the related service of subscriber is unprovisioned, not during subscriber removal. If subscriber has more than one service and we remove one of his services, then we remove MEs , but subscriber is still there with his remaining services. I think these MEs shoul be deleted in case all the services of the uni are removed.",
      "parentUuid": "289645d5_f6a254e0",
      "revId": "435d5541dcc6a0624aa0dd880eaf38f9dc414a44",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "990ebb29_de5f4649",
        "filename": "python/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_delete_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T18:23:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have a look at the openomci library state  machines, performance_intervals.py and the add_pm_me() function.  There is already an established pattern for setting up PM ME, but i dont think anything outside the library is using it yet.  \n\nIt looks to be event driven based on other ME being setup.  We may just need to let the library do more of the work.",
      "parentUuid": "e9263e6f_2c66164a",
      "revId": "435d5541dcc6a0624aa0dd880eaf38f9dc414a44",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f413dea6_bb547cbc",
        "filename": "python/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_delete_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-09T21:53:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also given these are created during the initial-mib-download stage they should not be deleted here.\n\nThere are other ME created during initial-mib-download that do not get deleted for the life of the ONU, and these could be the same.\n\nIf we truly want to delete these ME then we may need to create a separate openomci task to do this and have the delete performed as part of some explicit \"remove monitoring\" action.\n\nBut honestly i dont really see a need to delete the monitoring ME, just like we dont delete UNI MacBridge entries.",
      "parentUuid": "990ebb29_de5f4649",
      "revId": "435d5541dcc6a0624aa0dd880eaf38f9dc414a44",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
